## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-world streaming ingestion with multi-tenancy, schema evolution, and governance in AWS.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming ETL with Glue Spark
- Idempotent ingest and dedup via DynamoDB, partitioned Parquet
- Tenant isolation via Lake Formation
- Schema evolution and catalog management in Glue
- Data quality checks and end-to-end validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe in the Glue job
function process(record) {
  const key = record.tenant + '|' + record.event_id;
  if (!cache.has(key)) {
    writeParquet(record);
    cache.add(key);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and alert on schema drift across tenants?
- How would you test end-to-end with multiple tenants and evolving schemas?
